  "title": "Dataproc: Multi-Zone Clusters & Read-Only Field Updates",
  "summary": "Dataproc now supports multi-zone cluster configurations, enhancing resilience and availability. This release also includes breaking changes, making several fields in `ApplicationAttemptInfo` and `VirtualClusterOperationMetadata` read-only.",
  "details": "Developers can now configure multi-zone clusters using the new `multiZoneConfig` property within `GceClusterConfig`. This introduces the `MultiZoneConfig` schema, allowing instances to be distributed across multiple zones within a region, with `targetShape` (currently supporting `ANY`) to control distribution. This is a significant enhancement for cluster resilience.\n\n**Breaking Change Alert:** Several properties have been made read-only. If your code was previously setting these values, it will now fail. Specifically, `eventLogPath` in the `ApplicationAttemptInfo` schema is now read-only. Additionally, the following properties within the `VirtualClusterOperationMetadata` schema are now read-only: `createTime`, `description`, `doneTime`, `labels`, `operationType`, `virtualCluster`, `virtualClusterUuid`, and `warnings`. Please update your client code to reflect these changes.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
